- 2026-05-03: For `R(q, h_t)`, avoid a fixed global schema; use a minimal invariant envelope for audit/logging while optimizing the query-conditioned representation process itself.
- 2026-08-17: Pivot to harness-only training bed; v1 hermes runner was temporary.
- 2026-08-18: Live ledger training loop (plugin + host `/loop`/`/automate`); Claude-style plugin layout; in-place load; branch ships plugin + context only.
- 2026-08-19: Self-improving plugin: reflection may add skills, agents, tools, strategies; durable facts live in the overlay, not `graph-vault/`.
- 2026-08-19: Overlay is memory. Live problems may append revision claims (ADR 0008). Horizons lengthen across epochs; simulators only when a grade earns them.
- 2026-08-19: While the overlay is thin, discover overweights short resolution days (days–weeks) so reflection can score; keep a minority far analog clock per tick, not a 2027-heavy batch.
- 2026-08-19: Raise discover `K` to 15 to take more end-August / early-September clocks.
- 2026-08-19: Discover sets first Due; predict writes claim+justification (ADR 0009). Rename due-today → predict.
- 2026-08-19: Due and Y are one clock: resolution day on the problem; forecast day on each claim (ADR 0010).
- 2026-08-19: Long-term “how society works” modeling waits on plain-language locks in `docs/plans/2026-08-19-scale-forecast-roadmap.md`; scored events stay the test; no a-priori taxonomy.
- 2026-08-21: Architecture grill closed. Party-source first corpus: `references/party-sources.md` plus six live ledger rows from captions we could get (welcome, Saint-Denis, Tlaib, Mamdani, summit).
- 2026-08-21: Host ticker is already set as Cursor dashboard automations. Do not treat “arm the ticker” as unfinished. In-repo skills are the live procedure; dashboard prompts should follow those files.
- 2026-08-25: Home Amfis/DSA caption scrape done. Human job while the ticker runs is overlay review after graded series, not another tick. Hallway/on-site notes stay in chat unless already public.
- 2026-08-22: Tariff analog card has two clock phases: first deadline → delay prior; already-extended / post-pause clock → take-effect unless a new suspend instrument appears.
- 2026-08-24: On reflect, if a graded series named a later public answering date than **Resolution**, slide that heading later in the same tick so a freeze cannot drop the next phase off predict.
- 2026-08-30: Overlay is not markdown-only. The reflector writes the systems it needs (scripts, tests, small models, GNN) from the grade. It also **grades those systems** on the same series (keep / rewrite / cull), not only the claims. Ban is restoring parked trees (`graph-vault/`, France GNN), not a ban on deterministic code.

